<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>x09 Group Policy Templates</displayName>
  <description>Group Policy Templates for x09</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="RoleManagement_Name">Role Management via libnss-role</string>
      <string id="RoleManagement_Explain">Configure roles and privileges via libnss-role.

This policy allows managing group membership in groups on ALT Linux client machines.

Role file name:
Specify the file name (without path) that will be created in /etc/role.d/
Default: custom-roles.role
The file will be completely overwritten with the content from the role list below.

Role string format:
&lt;group&gt;:&lt;group&gt;[,&lt;group&gt;]*

where:
- left of the colon — role name (group that will be included in other groups)
- right of the colon — comma-separated list of groups this role is included in

Examples:
users: cdwriter, cdrom, audio, video, camera, floppy
localadmins: wheel
domain admins:localadmins
WIN\domain admins:localadmins
powerusers: remote, users

Allowed characters in group names:
- Latin, Cyrillic, digits
- symbols: \ - _ (backslash, hyphen, underscore)
- spaces

Each line in the list is one role. Group inclusions are applied recursively.</string>
      <string id="RoleFileName_Name">Role file name</string>
      <string id="RolesList_Name">Role list</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="RoleManagement">
        <textBox refId="RoleFileName">
          <label>Role file name (default: custom-roles.role):</label>
          <defaultValue>custom-roles.role</defaultValue>
        </textBox>
        <listBox refId="RolesList">Role list (format: role:group1,group2,...):</listBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
